$onText
Generated by nlp2mcp

This file contains the KKT (Karush-Kuhn-Tucker) conditions
for the original NLP model, transformed into MCP format.

KKT System Components:
  - Stationarity: ∇f + J^T λ + J^T ν - π^L + π^U = 0
  - Complementarity: g(x) ⊥ λ, h(x) = 0, bounds ⊥ π
  - Dual feasibility: λ, π^L, π^U ≥ 0
  - Primal feasibility: g(x) ≤ 0, h(x) = 0, lo ≤ x ≤ up
$offText

* ============================================
* Original Model Declarations
* ============================================

Sets
    nx /x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7, x8, x9, x10, x11, x12, x13, x14, x15, x16, x17, x18, x19, x20, x21, x22, x23, x24, x25, x26, x27, x28, x29, x30, x31, x32, x33, x34, x35, x36, x37, x38, x39, x40, x41, x42, x43, x44, x45, x46, x47, x48, x49, x50, x51/
    ny /y0, y1, y2, y3, y4, y5, y6, y7, y8, y9, y10, y11, y12, y13, y14, y15, y16, y17, y18, y19, y20, y21, y22, y23, y24, y25, y26/
;

Alias(nx, i);
Alias(ny, j);

Parameters
    D(nx,ny)
;

Scalars
    hx /0/
    hy /0/
    area /0/
    c /5/
;

hx = 1 / (card(nx) - 1);
hy = 1 / (card(ny) - 1);
D(i,j) = min(min(ord(i) - 1, card(nx) - ord(i)) * hx, min(ord(j) - 1, card(ny) - ord(j)) * hy);
area = 0.5 * hx * hy;

execError = 0;

* ============================================
* Variables (Primal + Multipliers)
* ============================================

* Primal variables: Original decision variables from the NLP
* Multipliers:
*   ν (nu_*): Free multipliers for equality constraints
*   λ (lam_*): Positive multipliers for inequality constraints
*   π^L (piL_*): Positive multipliers for lower bounds
*   π^U (piU_*): Positive multipliers for upper bounds

Variables
    v(nx,ny)
    stress
;

Positive Variables
    piL_v(nx,ny)
    piU_v(nx,ny)
;

* ============================================
* Variable Bounds
* ============================================

v.lo(i,j) = ((-1) * d(i,j));
v.up(i,j) = d(i,j);

* ============================================
* NLP Pre-Solve (warm-start for MCP duals)
* ============================================

$onMultiR
$include "data/gamslib/raw/torsion.gms"
$offMulti

* Transfer NLP duals to MCP multiplier initialization

* Transfer variable marginals to bound multipliers
piL_v.l(nx,ny)$(abs(v.l(nx,ny) - v.lo(nx,ny)) < 1e-6 and v.m(nx,ny) > 0) = v.m(nx,ny);
piU_v.l(nx,ny)$(abs(v.l(nx,ny) - v.up(nx,ny)) < 1e-6 and v.m(nx,ny) < 0) = -(v.m(nx,ny));

* Reset any NA/UNDF warm-start multiplier levels to 0 (#1322)
piL_v.l(nx,ny)$(NOT (piL_v.l(nx,ny) > -inf and piL_v.l(nx,ny) < inf)) = 0;
piU_v.l(nx,ny)$(NOT (piU_v.l(nx,ny) > -inf and piU_v.l(nx,ny) < inf)) = 0;

* ============================================
* Equations
* ============================================

* Stationarity: One equation per primal variable (except objvar)
* Complementarity: Equations for inequalities and bounds
* Equality constraints: Original equality constraints

Equations
    stat_v(nx,ny)
    comp_lo_v(nx,ny)
    comp_up_v(nx,ny)
    defstressx
;

* ============================================
* Equation Definitions
* ============================================

$onMultiR
* Stationarity equations
stat_v(nx,ny).. (sum((i,j), area * (2 * ((2 * (v(nx+1,ny) - v(nx,ny)) / hx * hx * (-1) / sqr(hx) + 2 * (v(nx,ny+1) - v(nx,ny)) / hy * hy * (-1) / sqr(hy)) * 1$(nx(i) and ny(j)) + (2 * (v(nx,ny) - v(nx-1,ny)) / hx * 1 / hx ** 1 + 2 * (v(nx,ny) - v(nx,ny-1)) / hy * 1 / hy ** 1) * 1$(nx(i) and ny(j))) / 4 - 3 * c * 2 * 1$(nx(i) and ny(j)) / 9)) - piL_v(nx,ny) + piU_v(nx,ny))$(v.up(nx,ny) - v.lo(nx,ny) > 1e-10) =E= 0;

* Lower bound complementarity equations
comp_lo_v(nx,ny)$(((-1) * d(nx,ny)) > -inf).. v(nx,ny) - ((-1) * d(nx,ny)) =G= 0;

* Upper bound complementarity equations
comp_up_v(nx,ny)$(d(nx,ny) < inf).. d(nx,ny) - v(nx,ny) =G= 0;

* Original equality equations
defstressx.. stress =E= area * ((sum((i,j)$(nx(i) and ny(j)), sqr((v(i+1,j) - v(i,j)) / hx) + sqr((v(i,j+1) - v(i,j)) / hy)) + sum((i,j)$(nx(i) and ny(j)), sqr((v(i,j) - v(i-1,j)) / hx) + sqr((v(i,j) - v(i,j-1)) / hy))) / 2 - c * (sum((i,j)$(nx(i) and ny(j)), v(i+1,j) + v(i,j) + v(i,j+1)) + sum((i,j)$(nx(i) and ny(j)), v(i,j) + v(i-1,j) + v(i,j-1))) / 3);

$offMulti

* ============================================
* Fix inactive variable instances
* ============================================

* Variables whose paired MCP equation is conditioned must be
* fixed for excluded instances to satisfy MCP matching.

v.fx(nx,ny)$(not (v.up(nx,ny) - v.lo(nx,ny) > 1e-10)) = v.lo(nx,ny);
piL_v.fx(nx,ny)$(not (v.up(nx,ny) - v.lo(nx,ny) > 1e-10)) = 0;
piU_v.fx(nx,ny)$(not (v.up(nx,ny) - v.lo(nx,ny) > 1e-10)) = 0;
piL_v.fx(nx,ny)$(not (((-1) * d(nx,ny)) > -inf)) = 0;
piU_v.fx(nx,ny)$(not (d(nx,ny) < inf)) = 0;

* ============================================
* Model MCP Declaration
* ============================================

* Each line pairs an equation with a variable:
*   equation.variable
*
* This defines the complementarity problem:
*   equation ⊥ variable
*
* Meaning: equation = 0 if variable > 0
*          equation ≥ 0 if variable = 0

Model mcp_model /
    stat_v.v,
    defstressx.stress,
    comp_lo_v.piL_v,
    comp_up_v.piU_v
/;

* ============================================
* Solve Statement
* ============================================

Solve mcp_model using MCP;

Scalar nlp2mcp_obj_val;
nlp2mcp_obj_val = stress.l;
Display nlp2mcp_obj_val;